# Cursor Rules for Comical-RS

## Project context
- Rust workspace with 5 crates: comical-core, comical-archive, comical-image, comical-app, comical-cli
- Desktop comic reader using eframe/egui + wgpu backend
- Pure-Rust archive support (ZIP, RAR, 7z) — no system dependencies
- Clean-room development: every commit must carry `Clean-Room: spec-v1` trailer

## Coding style
- Edition 2024, resolver v3
- Run `cargo fmt --all` before committing
- Run `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` — zero warnings policy
- Use `thiserror` for public error types; never panic on malformed input
- Document every `pub` item with doc comments
- Prefer builder patterns over positional arguments for >3 parameters
- Pin dependency versions; no wildcards

## Architecture constraints
- Read ARCHITECTURE.md at the start of every session
- comical-core is pure logic only — no I/O, no allocation beyond page lists
- comical-archive handles all archive formats behind a trait interface
- comical-image handles decode, probe, EXIF, resample, rotate
- comical-app owns UI state, caches, background workers
- Byte-budgeted LRU caches — respect cache_bytes and resample_bytes limits
- Background workers use crossbeam channels; rayon for CPU prefetch only

## Testing requirements
- Every new feature needs unit tests
- Image pipeline changes need golden vector updates in tests/vectors/
- Archive changes need corpus entries in tests/corpus/
- Run `cargo test --all` before committing
- Fuzz targets live in fuzz/ (excluded from workspace, nightly-only)

## Commit discipline
- Conventional Commits format: type(scope): description
- Every commit MUST include `Clean-Room: spec-v1` trailer
- Do not copy code from GPL/LGPL projects
- Do not reverse-engineer proprietary codecs
- Update docs/roadmap.md status table when completing milestones

## What NOT to do
- Do not add C/system dependencies without justification
- Do not use unsafe unless absolutely necessary (document why)
- Do not change the crate boundary responsibilities without updating ARCHITECTURE.md
- Do not remove or weaken existing tests
- Do not introduce unbounded allocations or memory leaks
- Do not default to purple/indigo/violet color palettes in UI code